  "description": "Dense Cooking transitions around the recorded Cream Stew route: Main handoffs, chef selection, recipe-page and retained-help changes, successful meal popup and dismissal, and field resumption.",
  "registration": "Reuse local/findings-menu/cooking-stew-main-transition-v1/dolphin without replaying Dolphin. Keep its unchanged paired fixture, disc, savestate prefix, RTC, inputs and capture profile. The controlled fixture learns recipe 15, grants ingredients and changes member vitals as recorded in cooking-stew-fixture-v1/fixture.json; this does not claim natural recipe acquisition or story progression. All 1,800 source observations have UI clock = 38084 + VI and effect clock = 37551 + VI. Register the complete source-observed ambient state at native update 64, including the initially empty poison-puff list and uninitialized gameplay RNG; every capture is native update = source VI + 64. Initial Y is native update 76, and later inputs use their observed source VI (poll / 2 + 1) + 64. The final Main close starts at update 1615 and field resumes at source VI 1563. The 191 captures retain all 15 original settled samples and their existing poison/paralysis checks, while adding dense Main/Cooking slides, chef selection, recipe-page and help changes, successful meal popup opening and dismissal, ignored movement during the held result, and field resumption. Source video timestamps were checked against the VI index; every requested VI is present. Persistent Cooking state, inventory, all nine members' vitals/conditions/training, effect clock/random state and gameplay RNG are checked at every capture. Cooking fade, scroll, previous recipe and popup opacity words were not observed by this older capture, so their transitions are checked through images only. Main viewport was also not observed, so no Main state gate is enabled. This route previews unknown recipe 14 but selects known recipe 15 before confirmation; it contains no error popup, no five-step recipe row scroll, and no Cooking reopen.",
